.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Onsager (1944) computed the free energy of the square-lattice Ising model exactly: the first exact solution of a model with a genuine phase transition. Ising2DOnsager evaluates his free energy, internal energy, and heat capacity, together with Yang&#x27;s (1952) spontaneous magnetization m=[1-\sinh^{-4}(2J/k_BT)]^{1/8}. The heat capacity diverges logarithmically at T_c, and the magnetization vanishes with exponent \beta=1/8. Neither the mean-field (Bragg-Williams) theory, shown for comparison, nor Ising&#x27;s own one-dimensional chain reproduces these features.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/statmech/ising/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_03_onsager_exact_solution_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/statmech/ising/plot_03_onsager_exact_solution`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Onsager's exact solution of the two-dimensional Ising model</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/statmech/ising/plot_03_onsager_exact_solution`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Boltzmann&#x27;s 1877 insight, written by Planck as S=k_B\ln W: entropy counts the microscopic arrangements W compatible with a macroscopic state. For N indistinguishable molecules on M lattice sites, W=\binom{M}{N}, and canonical_entropy evaluates k_B\ln W exactly via ln_binomial. The entropy is largest at half filling, where the number of arrangements peaks, and per site it converges to the Stirling-approximation mixing entropy -k_B[\theta\ln\theta+(1-\theta)\ln(1-\theta)] as M grows.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/statmech/lattice_gas/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_boltzmann_entropy_counting_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/statmech/lattice_gas/plot_02_boltzmann_entropy_counting`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Boltzmann's S = k ln W by counting lattice arrangements</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/statmech/lattice_gas/plot_02_boltzmann_entropy_counting`

